From: Trinity AI Agent <267220563+trinity-ai-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:10:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/11] TCSocket: always close the fd in Close(int)

Close(int fd) called close() only when shutdown() succeeded.
shutdown() fails with ENOTCONN when the peer has already reset the
connection, which is exactly when the link must be dropped. The fd then
leaked, stayed in m_Pfd, and ReConnect() never saw the module as
closed, so the module stayed dead.

Always close the descriptor and set the slot to -1. Log a shutdown()
error only when it is not ENOTCONN.
---
 TCSocket.cpp | 20 +++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/TCSocket.cpp b/TCSocket.cpp
index 20f6fbc..ba3c5f1 100644
--- a/TCSocket.cpp
+++ b/TCSocket.cpp
@@ -65,20 +65,18 @@ void CTCSocket::Close(int fd)
 	{
 		if (fd == p.fd)
 		{
-			if (shutdown(p.fd, SHUT_RDWR))
-			{
+			// shutdown() fails with ENOTCONN when the peer has already
+			// reset the link. The old code then skipped close(), leaked the
+			// descriptor and kept the dead fd, so the module never
+			// reconnected. Always close and always forget the fd.
+			if (shutdown(p.fd, SHUT_RDWR) && ENOTCONN != errno)
 				perror("shutdown");
-			}
-			else
+			if (close(p.fd))
 			{
-				if (close(p.fd))
-				{
-					std::cerr << "Error while closing " << fd << ": ";
-					perror("close");
-				}
-				else
-					p.fd = -1;
+				std::cerr << "Error while closing " << fd << ": ";
+				perror("close");
 			}
+			p.fd = -1;
 			return;
 		}
 	}
